# Desktop entries (/usr/share/applications/<id>) that get NoDisplay=true: they stay installed and
# keep working (file associations, "Open with…", D-Bus activation) but do not appear in Apps/Search.
# Hiding is used instead of removal wherever removing could break something.

# Second app store; the App Center (Bazaar) is the one store the owner sees.
org.kde.discover.desktop
org.kde.discover.flatpak.desktop
# Developer/admin tools that a Mac owner would never expect in the app list
org.kde.kate.desktop
htop.desktop
nvtop.desktop
org.kde.kdebugsettings.desktop
org.kde.kjournaldbrowser.desktop
org.kde.partitionmanager.desktop
org.kde.kmenuedit.desktop
org.kde.kwalletmanager.desktop
org.kde.kcolorschemeeditor.desktop
org.kde.kfontview.desktop
org.kde.keditbookmarks.desktop
org.kde.knetattach.desktop
org.kde.drkonqi.coredump.gui.desktop
org.kde.kdeconnect.nonplasma.desktop
# Remote desktop servers: switched on from System Settings when wanted
org.kde.krfb.desktop
org.kde.krfb.virtualmonitor.desktop
org.kde.krdpserver.desktop
# System Settings' own second entry ("KDE-Systemeinstellungen"): it carries NotShowIn=KDE, which
# the shell's Apps/Search (Quickshell DesktopEntries) do not evaluate, so it appeared next to
# "Systemeinstellungen" (integration walkthrough). Hidden, it still serves its purpose (System
# Settings opened on one page).
kdesystemsettings.desktop
# Duplicates of Search / System Monitor / Files
org.kde.kfind.desktop
org.kde.filelight.desktop
org.kde.kcharselect.desktop
# Opened automatically when a file needs it (like the Mac's Archive Utility)
org.kde.ark.desktop
# Input-method setup tools (reachable from System Settings → Keyboard)
org.freedesktop.IBus.Setup.desktop
ibus-setup-anthy.desktop
ibus-setup-chewing.desktop
ibus-setup-hangul.desktop
ibus-setup-libbopomofo.desktop
ibus-setup-libpinyin.desktop
ibus-setup-m17n.desktop
ibus-setup-tb.desktop
ibus-setup-typing-booster.desktop
